  "notes": "Lauda Europe (Ryanair group, Malta AOC) flies A320s for Ryanair's network; the scheme is its own, not Ryanair's. Drawn from one clear left-side photo; the belly, winglets (A320 wingtip fences) and right side aren't measured. A red mark on the tailplane root seen in the photo isn't drawn. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on 9H-LOR (left, 2025-12-15), reading x between the doors' known places on the A320 shape and heights against the window line: LAUDA runs x 0.157-0.446 (from 0.185-0.425) and its capitals reach y ~0.51, a third of the way from the windows' top to the crown (it had been drawn to 0.77, cap 0.55 from 0.8). The cheatline is level, straight between its points. photo_trace's fit of this photo missed the aft door by 40 px (it put the camera 18° below), so it wasn't used.",
  "history": "New entry. The Lauda scheme followed the 2018-2020 'laudamotion' livery after the rebrand to Lauda."
}
